Subject: [PATCH] Drop the Impress SVG-export presentation engine in WASM builds

filter/source/svg/presentation_engine.js is converted by js2hxx.py into
svgscript.hxx (111 C string fragments) and linked into .rodata by svgexport.cxx.
It is the JavaScript animation/navigation runtime for interactive SVG slideshows
exported from Impress.

MEASURED in the shipped web/modules/documents/soffice.wasm: 415,703 bytes of
payload spread over 56 data segments (located by markers unique to that file:
window.SVGPathSeg, aSlideShow, SlideAnimations, NextEffectEventArray,
@libreofficeend, PriorityQueue). Zeroing exactly those segment payloads and
re-running brotli -q 11 drops the module from 20,483,909 to 20,433,251 bytes:

    wire cost of the blob = 50,658 bytes

That is per module, and the blob is present in every module (documents is a
Writer-only build and carries it regardless), so the fix is worth roughly 5x
that across the shipped set.

WHY IT IS UNREACHABLE - the blob's only consumer is implGenerateScript(), called
from exactly one place, svgexport.cxx implExportDocument():

    if( mbPresentation && !mbExportShapeSelection )
        implGenerateScript();

mbPresentation is assigned in exactly one place, implExportImpressOrDraw():

    mbPresentation = Reference< XPresentationSupplier >(mxSrcDoc, UNO_QUERY).is();

and implExportImpressOrDraw() is only reached when !mbWriterFilter &&
!mbCalcFilter. So emitting the script requires an Impress document being written
THROUGH the SVG export filter. This product never exports SVG from any module -
web/js/format_registry.js contains no SVG entry, and SVG is offered as neither
an input nor an output format.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT TOUCH - embedded-SVG *import*. Images inside DOCX/ODT/RTF
render through a completely separate library: vcl/source/filter/graphicfilter.cxx
(IMP_SVG -> readSVG) builds a VectorGraphicData, which instantiates
com.sun.star.graphic.SvgTools, implemented in svgio (svgio/source/svguno/
xsvgparser.cxx). svgio does not link svgfilter and svgfilter does not link
svgio. svgfilter's own "ImportFilter" service is only "open a standalone .svg as
a Draw/Impress document"; it requires an XDrawPagesSupplier and then delegates
to GraphicFilter::ImportGraphic anyway.

This is deliberately the narrow cut. It removes the JS blob only and leaves the
svgfilter library, its .component and all five *_svg_Export.xcu registrations
in place, so no service registration becomes unresolvable.

NOT COMPILE-TESTED - no build was available. The failure mode if wrong is a
compile error in svgexport.cxx, which is loud and cheap.

VERIFY AFTER BUILDING:
  grep -c 'window.SVGPathSeg' web/modules/documents/soffice.wasm   # expect 0
and confirm soffice.wasm.br drops by ~50 KB.

--- a/filter/source/svg/svgexport.cxx
+++ b/filter/source/svg/svgexport.cxx
@@ -21,7 +21,9 @@
 #include "svgwriter.hxx"
 #include "svgfontexport.hxx"
 #include "svgfilter.hxx"
+#ifndef __EMSCRIPTEN__
 #include <svgscript.hxx>
+#endif
 
 #include <com/sun/star/awt/Rectangle.hpp>
 #include <com/sun/star/animations/XAnimationNodeSupplier.hpp>
@@ -1747,6 +1749,27 @@
 
 void SVGFilter::implGenerateScript()
 {
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    // WASM: do not embed the Impress SVG-export presentation engine.
+    //
+    // filter/source/svg/presentation_engine.js is converted by js2hxx.py into
+    // svgscript.hxx (111 string fragments) and linked into .rodata. Measured in
+    // the shipped documents module: 415,703 bytes of payload, costing 50,658
+    // bytes of wire after brotli -q 11.
+    //
+    // It is unreachable in this converter. The only caller of this function is
+    // gated on mbPresentation (implExportDocument), which is set solely in
+    // implExportImpressOrDraw() from an XPresentationSupplier query on the
+    // source document -- so it requires an Impress document being written
+    // THROUGH the SVG export filter. No module offers SVG as an output format
+    // (web/js/format_registry.js has no SVG entry), so no conversion this
+    // product performs can reach it.
+    //
+    // Embedded-SVG *import* is unaffected: DOCX/ODT images go through
+    // vcl/source/filter/graphicfilter.cxx -> readSVG -> VectorGraphicData ->
+    // com.sun.star.graphic.SvgTools, which is implemented in svgio and does not
+    // link svgfilter at all.
+#else
     mpSVGExport->AddAttribute(u"type"_ustr, u"text/ecmascript"_ustr);
 
     {
@@ -1761,6 +1784,7 @@
             }
         }
     }
+#endif
 }
 
 
